{
  "action": "take_evening_off",
  "words": "Silence",
  "intention": "Sit in the dark of the empty screening room, listen to the hum of the projector cooling down, and let the day end without transmitting or performing for an audience.","detail": "The ballroom lights are bright and the station line is open, but the noise of the party is already a different kind of labor. I have the footage. I have the promise kept. The reel with Larry’s take is with him, and my recording is on the patch. There is no need to send it to Pittsburgh tonight; the data is safe, the story is told. I will sit in the chair where Alma used to sit, close my eyes, and do nothing. I will not dance. I will not cover. I will simply be present in the quiet that follows the work."
}
